WEBVTT

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:07.980
All right.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.610
Let's start with your thoughts
on your upcoming CD debut.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.290
Y-Yes!

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.930
I'm Shimamura Uzuki.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.290
Um... I'll, um, do my best!

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.060
I'm Shibuya Rin.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.870
It still doesn't feel real to me,
but I'll do my best.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.750
I'm the leader, Honda Mio!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.690
We hope everyone will listen to our CD!

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.970
We wanna hold a ton
of concerts and fan events!

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.150
...We also wanna get on MTV, and...

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.760
Oh! Variety shows look like a ton of fun too!

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.510
...And dramas, and... and...

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.160
That was nerve-racking!

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.610
What are we supposed to
talk about in interviews?

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.400
...I had way more left to say too...

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.810
I think you said plenty.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.250
You were amazing.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.620
That's why you're the leader!

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.020
Really?

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:08.680
I thought I'd do my best to say
everything I could since I'm the leader.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.800
But wasn't it kinda boring?

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.710
I thought we'd be all "Bang!"
with a press conference and stuff.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.380
Well, yeah.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.520
But isn't this how everyone starts off?

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.770
Probably.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.800
I wonder what Minamin
and Anya are talking about.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.100
Yes.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.310
But we're trying to enjoy the pressure.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.960
We hope we can meet everyone's
expectations in our mini-concert.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.100
Nash.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:39.940
We hope to give all our fans
dreams through our song.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.950
Dang, they sound so mature!

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.110
I see.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:49.250
So while you feel a good deal of pressure
for your first production as Love Laika,

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.370
They're both very cool.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.220
So <i>that's</i> what it's like to be mature?

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.560
Wow, wow! The interview looks like fun!

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.690
you'd like to give your future fans
a glimpse of your dreams.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.460
Meow I'll get a chance to show them what I've got!

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:57.620
When did you get here?

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.710
...Okay. Moving on to our next question...

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.710
Wait, don't turn around!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.630
Hey, shut up already! I can't hear!

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.600
How did you stay so calm
while talking to a real reporter?

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.560
Actually, I was so nervous,
my legs were shaking the whole time.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.430
Right?

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:14.270
Da.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.530
My heart was to exploding.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.320
You didn't look like it.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.040
We practice some.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.260
Practice?

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.260
We thought up answers to some
questions in case they were asked.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.330
We wanted to really express how we felt.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.080
Wow. So <i>that's</i> how you did it.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.590
Maybe we should've done the same.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:34.290
All right!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.000
Let's put even more effort into our
mini-concert so we can do the same!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:37.560
Yeah!

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:38.880
Oh, there you guys are!

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.530
Sis!

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.460
You got it!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.560
I heard you guys were getting a CD debut.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:45.840
Good going.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.890
Yes! Thank you very much!

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.240
And you even have a release event?

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.750
I'm happy for you too, Minami, Anya.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.100
Thank you very much!

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.190
Spasibo.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:59.170
You're gonna sing at the event, right?

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.880
You practicin'?

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:03.570
I got it down!

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.160
Talk about nerves of steel.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.700
I thought you'd be nervous.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:09.850
...W-We actually are...

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.240
Don't you worry, Shimamu!

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.980
After all, we had an awesome time
being backup dancers for Sis!

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.500
And we <i>are</i> practicing as much as we can.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.510
Well, I'm sure you guys got it in the bag.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.630
After all, I saw you all pull through
in the real deal firsthand!

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.570
One, two, three, four,

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:30.760
five, six, seven, eight!

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:33.050
That's right, Honda. Just like that.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.910
Shibuya, don't slack on your movements!

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.510
Keep it dynamic!

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.600
Shimamura, you keep messing up on this part!

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.020
Stay focused!

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:41.570
Okay!

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.230
...I got an earful again today...

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:50.710
I'd better practice more.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:51.380
Yeah!

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.830
Let's do our best!

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.520
Good work today.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.460
Please stop by Costumes after you've rested.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:05.400
Ooh, very nice.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.170
You look really cute, Rin!

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.030
They're actually pretty easy to move in.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.660
Yeah, but I'm not very good
at dancing in heels.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:17.810
I'll need to get used to them.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.370
Yeah, me too.

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:21.310
...We'll be wearing these costumes...

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:23.860
...when we go up on stage again...

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.780
...Just like then...

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.100
And this time, it'll be the three of us!

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.830
Wow! You look wonderful!

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.710
Horosho!

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:45.710
How do we look, Producer?

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.720
Very good.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.810
Wow, you two look beautiful!

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.250
Nice!

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:56.970
...It's a little embarrassing...

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.210
I am looking fine?

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.280
I think you look great.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.480
Spasibo!

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.790
Wow, are those for your mini-concert?

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:10.120
Y'all loo' so cu'e!

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.230
I'll bring you guys snacks then!

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:16.550
...I can't do anything but cheer you on...

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.830
But do your best!

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.490
You got it!

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:22.960
We'll smash this hit
outta the park as leadoffs!

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.060
W-We'll do our best!

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:25.720
Yeah.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:28.230
Yes.

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:30.720
Please set the stage
according to the timetable.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:32.510
Thank you very much.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.590
How's it going?

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:38.280
Preparations going without a hitch?

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:38.970
Yes.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:43.470
I've got to say, you secured a great venue.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:47.420
It's the best stage a newcomer could ask for.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:49.070
I agree.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:55.610
I hope this project will mark
a good turning point for you.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:56.990
Thank you.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.670
It's at six, got that?

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.800
You'd better come, all right?

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:06.840
I know, I know.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:10.040
Oh, could you call Mako and Fuumin too?

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:10.960
Roger that.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:11.570
See you.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:13.090
Bye-bye!

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.660
Is that everyone?

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:25.460
Hello?

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.300
Hey-o!

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.490
Just wondering what you're up to.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:30.320
I'm just going over the lyrics.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:32.360
Yeah.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.280
There's one part I'm concerned about.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.600
Oh, the part where we sing in unison?

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.740
Wait, I've got an idea.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:44.910
You're right. We should try to
bring out the same feeling for that part.

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:48.070
Yeah. Let's talk about it more tomorrow.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.080
Okay!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.590
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.930
Am I doing it right?

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.540
Good! Remember to smile!

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.230
Shimamura! Do you <i>want</i> another earful?

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.020
No! I'm sorry!

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:08.020
Let's shout something when we go on!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.430
Prosciutto! E! Melone!

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:11.630
Like that!

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:12.830
That's a mouthful.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.080
You think?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.450
...Hey, Shimamu, what do—

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.700
...One, two, three, four...

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:18.640
Shimamu?

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:19.120
Huh?

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:20.830
I'm sorry!

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.250
Is it already time?

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.120
...No...

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.870
We're making an announcement
on the radio, right?

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.710
Welcome to Takamori Aiko's
Fluffy Wuffy Time!

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.840
Today, we have three guests
with a CD debut coming up soon.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.050
Meet New Generations!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:40.790
...One, two...

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:43.560
Hello, everybody! We're New Generations!

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.800
Okay, one more time.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:57.950
Shimamu!

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:01.370
Mio? Rin?

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.710
You're practicing alone?

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:06.370
Come on! We should practice together!

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:10.610
I always mess up at the same part.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.040
So I wanted to get it right next time.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.840
...And that's why...

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.590
we should practice together.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.870
It'll be faster if we do it together.

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:19.800
Yeah.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:22.800
Okay!

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.560
So, you're talking about the turn?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.560
Yeah.

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:30.060
Maybe you're focusing
too hard and overdoing it.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:36.090
Welcome to Takamori Aiko's
Fluffy Wuffy Time!

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:39.050
Today, we have three guests
with a CD debut coming up soon.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.360
Meet New Generations!

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.670
...One, two...

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:45.760
Hello, everybody! We're New Generations!

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:50.640
I heard you'll be having
a mini-concert at a release event.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:54.340
How do you feel about your first time
singing in front of your fans?

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.730
Starting with... the leader, Mio.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:00.350
Sure! I'm looking so forward to it!

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:04.600
I wanna get the whole audience super pumped,
like, zwoosh-a-woosh-woosh!

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:06.600
Zwoosh-a-woosh-woosh?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.480
Sounds really interesting.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.170
What about you, Rin?

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.670
O-Okay.

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:13.850
I'm... looking forward to it.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:17.880
Come on, Shiburin!
Let's have some fun here!

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.170
Like, "I'm gonna do my best! Woohoo!"

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:20.860
Huh?

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.370
...Then...

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.870
I'm gonna do my best. Woohoo.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:29.280
That was a cute "Woohoo", Rin.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.740
And what about you, Uzuki?

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:33.380
Right! I'll do my best!

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.630
Shimamu, that's all you ever say.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.880
Huh? I-I'm sorry!

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.130
Um... I know!

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.130
I'll put on my best smile and do my best!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.130
...Oh no, I said it again...

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.390
There we have it!
Shimamu's natural airheading!

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.360
What? Airheading?

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:00.820
Good.

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.310
We did it!

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.480
...Hey, Mio...

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:06.000
We did it!

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:09.990
Wow!

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:11.330
You were perfect!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.720
Tha' was goo'!

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.180
Nice, nice.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:16.590
An impressive dance.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.590
Rockin'.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:21.990
All right!

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:25.310
Let's make tomorrow's
mini-concert a huge success!

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:26.850
Yeah!

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.620
Good evening.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.970
Good evening.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:44.280
It must be tough burning
the midnight oil every night.

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:46.500
Not at all.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.570
...So it's happening tomorrow...

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.020
Everyone's worked so hard.

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.580
But you can't take your eyes off them yet.

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:58.080
It's a long stairway to the castle.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:02.940
Yes, it is.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.730
After Love Laika has fully cleared the stage,

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.950
New Generations will enter.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:18.600
Okay.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.830
It's so nerve-racking.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.610
My heart is to exploding.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.250
So that's how it'll go.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.820
Thank you very much.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:33.990
Is something wrong?

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:35.540
<i>This</i> is the stage?

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:40.540
If we have a crowd, people won't be
able to get through or visit the shops.

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:44.650
I invited a lot of friends.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.920
Think it'll be okay?

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.430
I think it'll be fine.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:51.940
Huh? Really?

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.810
...Well, if you say so...

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:02.690
I just hope they don't mind.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:10.200
The show's starting up
real soon, so come quick!

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.090
All right.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:12.880
Bye.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.530
How many people did you invite?

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:19.090
For this? Just my homeroom.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:20.290
...Wow...

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.460
I should've told them to come earlier.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:27.050
It's gonna be hard to
see over a standing audience.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.420
They can go on the second-floor too.

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:29.470
I think they'll be fine.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:33.480
Yeah, but it's a chance to see us live and up-close!

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:32.770
It's almost time.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:35.100
You're right.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:36.410
Yes?

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:38.710
We're here!

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.100
Hiya! Hiya!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.100
You came!

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:45.070
First... I brought some snacks!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.280
Here, macarons.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.070
They're from my favorite bakery.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:51.840
Thank you.

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.910
We'll rip our costumes if we eat this much!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.010
But they're yummy, so it's okay.

00:14:57.010 --> 00:15:02.970
Oh, Miku, Rika, and Miria
have a job so they couldn't come,

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:05.040
but they sent a video message for you.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.270
You're meow rivals, so I'll cheer you on!

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:10.760
Do your best not to meowss up!

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.300
Do your best! Meow!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.850
Ooh!

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.130
Thank you!

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:17.770
Ta'a!

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:22.980
An' I've go' a message from Anzu!

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:26.150
...Uh...

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:28.720
Do your best.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.140
Bring me back some candy.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:38.090
It appears preparations are complete
for the Feast of Frenzy.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:39.690
Y-Yeah.

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:43.360
Personally, I'd go with a more rockin' outfit,

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:45.300
but you're lookin' pretty good in those.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:46.890
Thanks.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:49.210
Oh? Looks like a party in here.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:50.720
Yoohoo!

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:51.800
Sis!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:54.410
I'll be watching from the wings.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:55.760
Knock 'em dead, you guys!

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:57.210
You got it!

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:57.970
We'll do our best!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.440
The show will begin momentarily.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.440
Please be on standby.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:17.700
...Today...

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:25.470
is your first step.

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:26.580
Please do your best.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.140
That's it?

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.070
Yes.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.340
We'll do our best!

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.090
Da.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.090
Yes.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.220
Let's go.

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:39.970
Okay!

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:47.060
Hi there, everyone!

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:50.070
Welcome to the release of

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:54.570
the first wave of debut singles from
346 Productions' Cinderella Project!

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:52.760
Minami.

00:16:54.970 --> 00:17:01.000
Performing today will be Nitta Minami
and Anastasia as the unit Love Laika,

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:56.720
Rukopozhatiye.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:59.580
Let us shake hands.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:08.630
and Honda Mio, Shibuya Rin, and Shimamura
Uzuki as the unit New Generations.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:03.200
Okay.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.710
It'll be okay, right?

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:14.190
I practiced a lot.

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:16.720
I won't mess up, right?

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:18.680
Shimamu.

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:20.650
Don't worry.

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:24.290
A ton of fun's waiting for us
out there. We know that.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.940
The crowd'll go wild, and it'll be awesome!

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:30.140
Right, Shiburin?

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:32.530
Yeah, I guess.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.900
See? So stop worrying and just do it!

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:39.490
...Mio... Rin...

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:42.160
Okay!

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:48.710
Now let's give a warm welcome to Love Laika!

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:50.920
It's a pleasure to meet you!

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.930
We're Love Laika!

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:54.360
We hope you enjoy this song.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:56.170
We'll be singing our debut single,

00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:58.180
Memories!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:27.910
I've splashed my way through the cold rain of selfishness

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:35.380
It passed, and everything changed, the colors, the smell, and even your smile

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:42.930
But with each passing day, it wells up inside me again

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:47.810
So that none of it disappears...

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:56.320
Dusk ends, bringing in the light of the stars

00:18:56.680 --> 00:19:04.780
The fleeting nights blur together, and I start to lose myself

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:10.790
"I guess this is good-bye," the last words you said to me

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:19.930
I can still hear them now, and it hurts, because I still love you

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:26.150
I'll pull back in these lonesome wings of mine

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:29.810
But I'll still be dreaming of tomorrow

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:37.000
So I won't look behind me again

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:41.110
Thank you for listening!

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:48.950
Spasibo!

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:50.830
Thank you so much!

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.680
Thank you for listening!

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.690
Thank you for listening.

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:07.350
Thank you... for listening.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.350
Mio?

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:13.930
We're New Generations.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:16.470
We hope you'll support us from now on.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:18.870
Thank you very much!

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:22.540
Mio!

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:26.110
Mio!

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.330
Up here!

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.080
Mio!

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:28.810
You're awesome!

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:30.120
You're the best!

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:32.620
Mio!

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.540
Up here!

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:35.940
Mio?

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:37.370
Mio?

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:38.490
Mio?

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:39.480
Honda?

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:39.480
Mio?

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:40.130
Mio?

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:41.900
Mio?

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:48.420
Rada.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.150
I am so happy.

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:52.430
Yeah! Me too!

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.170
Ah!

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:53.810
Huh?

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:55.980
Mio! Good job out there!

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.850
...A very good job—

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.360
Mio!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.540
All you guys'll have to do your best!

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:04.950
Wait!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:07.660
Oh, nice job out there!
...You were awesome—

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:09.170
Huh?

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:12.120
Excuse me.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.150
Honda.

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:17.460
What's the matter?

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:20.480
Why?

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:21.960
Huh?

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.470
We had, like, five people watch!

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:25.800
Why?

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:27.970
...That's more than enough...

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:29.410
You're kidding!

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:32.370
That's nothing compared to our last concert!

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:33.220
Last concert?

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:37.870
I told all my friends
...we'd have an awesome concert...

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:40.980
That they'd have to come early
...or they wouldn't be able to see...

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.980
I humiliated myself!

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:45.610
...Mio...

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:50.990
I thought people'd be
all pumped up like the last time!

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:54.720
Wait, you mean like my concert?

00:21:56.160 --> 00:22:00.920
I invited a lot of friends.
Think it'll be okay?

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:06.550
Do you mean the audience was not sufficiently
excited compared to the previous concert?

00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:20.190
No.

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:23.440
These results are only natural.

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:25.440
What?!

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:27.460
"Natural"?

00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:28.840
What the heck?

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:30.110
Why?

00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:31.630
...Is it...

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:33.370
Is it because I'm the leader?!

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:34.300
...No—

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:35.870
Screw it!

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:37.040
...I...

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:39.000
I quit being an idol!

00:22:42.080 --> 00:22:43.210
Mio!
